em-central-simple-algebra}", "REF_0003": "\\cite{SilvermanEllipticCurves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}[", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ecc03e3d9a992795498006dd7a8ceb4955ebeb6f108807908b474d4cedda779c", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:0fffd42f934ba53d7059533a5d4d7291f8e6b675b7abd650ac0130890af749aa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:23bb1bfddcd09307295172c9a238c13dedbc223715a0e89b63b1059058cbb7ed", "source_text": "Sketch of proof.<PROOFARGEND_0001>The Skolem-Noether theorem (see\nBrauer Groups, Theorem <REF_0001>)\nimplies that for any field <MATH_0001> the group\n<MATHSEG_0001>-Algebras<MATHSEG_0002>\nequals <MATH_0002>. By\nTheorem <REF_0002>, we see that\ncentral simple algebras of degree <MATH_0003> correspond\nto forms of the <MATH_0004>-algebra <MATH_0005>.\nCombined we see that isomorphism classes of degree <MATH_0006> central\nsimple algebras correspond to elements of\n<MATH_0007>.\nFor more details on twisting, see for example\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eebc15b10d8982ec288448cf6ec1953158dd7f50968656ef83dac0d0985ad8b4", "unit_id": "tag:03R6:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03R1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$d$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$\\xi_A$", "MATH_0005": "$H^1(\\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), \\text{PGL}_d(K^{sep}))$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n1 \\to (K^{sep})^* \\to \\text{GL}_d(K^{sep}) \\to \\text{PGL}_d(K^{sep}) \\to 1,\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\delta_d :\nH ^1(\\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), \\text{PGL}_d(K^{sep}))\n\\longrightarrow\nH^2(\\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), (K^{sep})^*).\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0009": "$(g_\\sigma)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\delta_d(\\xi)$", "MATH_0011": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-two-cocycle}\n(\\sigma, \\tau)\n\\longmapsto\n\\tilde g_\\sigma^{-1} \\tilde g_{\\sigma \\tau} \\sigma(\\tilde g_\\tau^{-1})\n\\in (K^{sep})^*\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0012": "$\\tilde g_\\sigma \\in \\text{GL}_d(K^{sep})$", "MATH_0013": "$g_\\sigma$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\delta : \\text{Br}(K) \\longrightarrow H^2(\\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K), (K^{sep})^*),\n\\quad\n[A] \\longmapsto \\delta_{\\deg A} (\\xi_A)\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$A$", "MATH_0016": "$d$", "MATH_0017": "$K$", "MATH_0018": "$\\varphi : \\text{Mat}_d(K^{sep}) \\to A \\otimes_K K^{sep}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\sigma \\in \\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K)$", "MATH_0020": "$\\tilde g_\\sigma \\in \\text{GL}_d(K^{sep})$", "MATH_0021": "$\\varphi^{-1} \\circ \\sigma(\\varphi)$", "MATH_0022": "$x \\mapsto \\tilde g_\\sigma x \\tilde g_\\sigma^{-1}$", "MATH_0023": "$H^2$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-two-cocycle}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9952cc85ee4bc7037cbb1bb660517c9afd838e1304f9bfc3d0bef464ba9459f1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c5009b11b946ed80ef1cdadb7dcf758087af9ca203fced580421508074d6278d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> is a finite central simple algebra of degree <MATH_0002> over a field <MATH_0003>,\nwe denote <MATH_0004> the corresponding cohomology class in\n<MATH_0005>.\nConsider the short exact sequence\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich gives rise to a long exact cohomology sequence (up to degree 2) with\ncoboundary map\n<MATH_0007>\nExplicitly, this is given as follows: if <MATH_0008> is a cohomology class\nrepresented by the 1-cocycle <MATH_0009>, then <MATH_0010> is the\nclass of the 2-cocycle\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> is a lift of <MATH_0013>.\nUsing this we can make explicit the map\n<MATH_0014>\nas follows. Assume <MATH_0015> has degree <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>. Choose an isomorphism\n<MATH_0018>. For\n<MATH_0019> choose an element\n<MATH_0020> such that\n<MATH_0021> is equal to the map\n<MATH_0022>. The class in <MATH_0023>\nis defined by the two cocycle (<REF_0001>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f73c6838900861f26db32ac30419ee90a8c42cff12d0a004a174b1849e08972", "unit_id": "tag:03R1:prose-0004"}
